WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.103 --> 00:00:19.266
Outside, Scrooge walked along, greeting everyone on the streets with a delighted smile.

2
00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:24.088
A pair of men noticed his joy and smiled in return.

3
00:00:24.108 --> 00:00:26.129
"Good morning, sir!"

4
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:28.311
one said, tipping his hat.

5
00:00:29.451 --> 00:00:30.592
"Merry Christmas to you."

6
00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:36.370
"Thank you, sir, and I wish you the same," Scrooge said.

7
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.392
He hadn't gone much farther when he spotted one of the gentlemen who had visited his office the

8
00:00:42.432 --> 00:00:42.992
day before.

9
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.913
It sent a pang through his heart now.

10
00:00:47.654 --> 00:00:52.096
Scrooge had sent him away, yelling horribly about putting poor people in prison.

11
00:00:52.116 --> 00:00:55.577
"My dear sir!"

12
00:00:56.778 --> 00:00:58.899
Scrooge hurried to catch up to the gentleman.

13
00:00:58.919 --> 00:01:01.700
"A merry Christmas to you!"

14
00:01:04.112 --> 00:01:05.333
"Mr. Scrooge?"

15
00:01:05.793 --> 00:01:07.354
the gentleman said in surprise.

16
00:01:07.374 --> 00:01:11.996
"That's my name," Scrooge said.

17
00:01:12.016 --> 00:01:15.739
"Though I fear you may not think much of it.

18
00:01:16.579 --> 00:01:21.001
Still, I hope a generous donation to the poor will change your mind."

19
00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.584
He whispered an amount of money into the man's ear.

20
00:01:27.345 --> 00:01:29.026
The man's eyes went wide.

21
00:01:29.046 --> 00:01:32.688
"Mr. Scrooge, are you serious?

22
00:01:33.908 --> 00:01:36.169
You want to donate all that money?"

23
00:01:36.189 --> 00:01:41.290
"I am serious," Scrooge said.

24
00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.591
"Not a penny less.

25
00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:48.552
Will you please do me the favor of accepting it, and seeing that it helps the poor?"

26
00:01:48.572 --> 00:01:52.373
"I will, of course!

27
00:01:52.874 --> 00:01:53.394
Thank you!"

28
00:01:55.054 --> 00:01:56.034
Scrooge nodded.

29
00:01:56.054 --> 00:01:59.095
"Come to see me at my office tomorrow.

30
00:01:59.736 --> 00:02:00.836
I'll give you the money then."

31
00:02:03.708 --> 00:02:08.812
Scrooge continued on his way, patting children on the head and giving coins to beggars.

32
00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:14.115
"What a wonderful, beautiful holiday!"

33
00:02:14.516 --> 00:02:15.056
he thought.

34
00:02:17.878 --> 00:02:19.779
Finally he reached his nephew's house.

35
00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.142
He wanted to stop and knock but his knees trembled.

36
00:02:28.065 --> 00:02:32.388
He had to pass by the door a dozen times before he finally found the courage to knock.

37
00:02:35.912 --> 00:02:37.873
A servant brought him to the dining room.

38
00:02:39.273 --> 00:02:44.835
Scrooge peered nervously into the room filled with Fred and his family, as well as some guests.

39
00:02:47.635 --> 00:02:49.296
"Why, bless my soul!

40
00:02:49.596 --> 00:02:50.176
Who's that?"

41
00:02:50.596 --> 00:02:51.236
Fred said.

42
00:02:51.256 --> 00:02:57.478
"I've I've Scrooge's voice quaked.

43
00:02:59.299 --> 00:03:01.179
"I've, um, come to dinner.

44
00:03:01.199 --> 00:03:03.840
Will you let me in, Fred?"

45
00:03:06.132 --> 00:03:06.793
"Of course!"

46
00:03:08.174 --> 00:03:11.337
Fred took his uncle's hand and nearly shook Scrooge's arm off.

47
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.662
The family immediately made Scrooge feel at home.

48
00:03:17.744 --> 00:03:20.626
He was welcomed by Fred's wife and by their children.

49
00:03:22.348 --> 00:03:24.210
Other guests chatted politely with him.

50
00:03:25.831 --> 00:03:30.116
It was a wonderful party, with delicious food and entertaining games.

51
00:03:31.668 --> 00:03:34.269
Scrooge stayed late and enjoyed himself thoroughly.

52
00:03:39.351 --> 00:03:42.613
Even so, he was up early the next morning to go to work.

53
00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:47.034
In fact, he arrived even earlier than usual.

54
00:03:47.054 --> 00:03:51.696
"Good," he thought as he sat at his desk.

55
00:03:51.716 --> 00:03:54.077
"Cratchit isn't here yet.

56
00:03:55.498 --> 00:03:57.379
I hope he comes in late this morning."

57
00:03:59.219 --> 00:04:00.060
And so he did.

58
00:04:01.128 --> 00:04:04.691
Cratchit was a full 18 minutes late when he finally arrived.

59
00:04:06.192 --> 00:04:10.675
He rushed in, leaping onto his stool as if he were trying to catch up with the clock.

60
00:04:13.717 --> 00:04:17.060
"What do you mean by showing up here at this time of day?"

61
00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.621
Scrooge growled.

62
00:04:18.641 --> 00:04:22.824
"I'm sorry, sir," Cratchit said meekly.

63
00:04:22.844 --> 00:04:27.888
"I My family and I "Step this way!"

64
00:04:29.856 --> 00:04:32.799
Cratchit cowered as he followed his boss across the room.

65
00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:36.281
"It's only once a year, sir.

66
00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:38.283
It won't happen again."

67
00:04:38.303 --> 00:04:45.249
"Well, the current way of doing things around here is unacceptable," Scrooge snapped.

68
00:04:45.269 --> 00:04:52.715
"And therefore He couldn't stop a smile from taking the place of his angry scowl.

69
00:04:52.735 --> 00:04:56.058
"I'm going to raise your salary!

70
00:04:57.099 --> 00:04:58.400
Merry Christmas, Bob!"

71
00:04:59.988 --> 00:05:01.829
Cratchit gazed at him in amazement.

72
00:05:01.849 --> 00:05:04.110
"Are you serious, Mr.

73
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:08.472
Scrooge?" Scrooge clapped him on the back.

74
00:05:08.492 --> 00:05:12.993
"I haven't given you a very merry Christmas for many years now.

75
00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.294
But I wish to make up for that.

76
00:05:17.415 --> 00:05:21.277
I'll raise your salary, and do whatever I can to help your family.

77
00:05:22.297 --> 00:05:25.839
That includes hiring the best doctors for Tiny Tim."

78
00:05:25.859 --> 00:05:31.178
"But But Tears filled Cratchit's eyes.

79
00:05:31.198 --> 00:05:33.359
"Thank you, sir."

80
00:05:33.379 --> 00:05:37.363
"Don't thank me, Bob.

81
00:05:38.183 --> 00:05:42.287
Please go home to your family and take another day off!"

82
00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:47.251
Scrooge was as good as his word.

83
00:05:48.332 --> 00:05:53.976
Thanks to the doctors he hired, the tragic scene shown by the Ghost of Christmas Future never appeared.

84
00:05:57.379 --> 00:05:59.501
Instead Tiny Tim thrived.

85
00:06:01.062 --> 00:06:06.066
Not only that, but he also grew up thinking of Ebenezer Scrooge as a second father.

86
00:06:07.727 --> 00:06:10.689
And Scrooge didn't stop there, with the Cratchit family.

87
00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.992
Instead he became a charitable man.

88
00:06:16.893 --> 00:06:19.215
Everyone who knew him observed the same thing.

89
00:06:21.797 --> 00:06:26.320
He kept the kind and loving spirit of Christmas with him all year long.

90
00:06:29.268 --> 00:06:34.891
"That's what I strive for every day of my life," he said to anyone who asked him about

91
00:06:34.951 --> 00:06:40.333
it. "May that be said of all of us—that we are kind and loving.

92
00:06:41.954 --> 00:06:46.556
As Tiny Tim might say, God bless us, everyone!"
